Original commit body from fbd37c5c3205380f106af3f70ac790c26bc44507:

Three spec sites overclaimed byte-level reproducibility, contradicting the
spec's own reproducibility_context L2 disclaimer (spec:757-786):
  - :321  analysis_runs[] "byte-stable across runs"
  - :72   UX key principle "deterministic and reproducible given same repo state"
  - :1649 verification checklist "same input -> same output"

A two-run survey confirms the array is NOT byte-stable: 65/65 analysis_runs
entries carry a different execution_id (per-run uuid:) plus fresh wall-clock
started_at/duration_ms, and the whole-file sha256 differs; the node stable_id
set is identical (the L2 semantic graph reproduces). The pass ORDER also varies
run-to-run: started_at is microsecond wall-clock (65/65 distinct), so the sort
reflects real-time completion order -- WI-haguz removed the old random dict-order
but did not make the order reproducible.

All three sites now scope the guarantee to the L2 semantic graph (nodes, edges,
stable_ids, run_signature). Byte-level reproducibility remains a separate opt-in
(WI-sazap --reproducible). Docs-only; smart-test selects 0 tests.

